WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:04.004
♪♪

00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:07.758
(Thunder)

00:00:07.758 --> 00:00:13.222
(Wind blows)

00:00:13.222 --> 00:00:14.723
(Glass shatters)

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:21.480
(Intense music builds)

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:24.691
Susan:
After we survived Hurricane
Katrina...

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:28.737
Susan:
we thought that we could survive
anything.

00:00:29.071 --> 00:00:34.451
(Water rushing)

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.495
And we were wrong.

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:37.829
♪♪

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:40.832
Attorney General:
They found 45 dead bodies there.

00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:42.834
Attorney General:
Now does that make any sense
to you?

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:45.254
♪♪

00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:48.840
I'm under a great deal of
pressure to look into what
happened.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.928
Dr. Horace Baltz:
There were 5 days, the most
ungodly conditions.

00:00:52.928 --> 00:00:56.556
♪♪

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.725
Karen Wynn:
We are getting all of these
patients out of here.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.269
We are nurses,

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:00.978
Karen Wynn:
and we're gonna get it done.

00:01:00.978 --> 00:01:04.523
♪♪

00:01:04.523 --> 00:01:05.857
As long as we don't get left
behind.

00:01:05.857 --> 00:01:08.652
♪♪

00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:11.488
Dr. Ewing Cook:
We have to be realistic about
the situation.

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:13.573
♪♪

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.993
There is nothing else to do for
them.

00:01:16.994 --> 00:01:19.037
Dr. Anna Pou:
Except to make them comfortable.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.081
So what are we talking about?

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:25.210
♪♪

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:28.880
Schafer:
They've asked me to look 
into the deaths at Memorial Medical Center.

00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:29.881
Schafer:
Anna...

00:01:29.881 --> 00:01:33.302
Schafer:
The Attorney Generals Office is
focusing their investigation on you.

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:37.306
They're suggesting that some of
their patients' lives may have
been ended?

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:40.767
I am sure that patients do not
suffer pain.

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:42.477
♪♪

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.855
Dr. Bryant King:
Some people who were afraid of
people outside of the hospital.

00:01:44.855 --> 00:01:45.731
♪♪

00:01:45.731 --> 00:01:46.732
But for me...

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:48.275
Dr. Bryant King:
it was the other way around.

00:01:48.275 --> 00:01:49.359
♪♪

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:52.362
Dr. Ewing Cook:
If you were given the choice
between comforting a patient...

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:54.614
Dr. Ewing Cook:
possibly quickening his death,

00:01:55.157 --> 00:01:55.657
Dr. Ewing Cook:
or...

00:01:56.158 --> 00:01:57.451
♪♪

00:01:57.451 --> 00:01:59.995
Dr. Ewing Cook:
...abandoning patients to
suffer a slow death.

00:01:59.995 --> 00:02:02.497
♪♪

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:03.832
Dr. Ewing Cook:
What would you choose to do?

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:06.168
♪♪

00:02:06.168 --> 00:02:08.045
Let me say goodbye, please!

00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:08.962
Come on man! 

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:09.546
Stay back!

00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:11.173
(Sirens)

00:02:11.173 --> 00:02:13.258
♪♪

00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:16.303
Dr. Anna Pou:
All I did was try to help
people. That is all I did.

00:02:16.303 --> 00:02:20.349
♪♪

